.Dd $Mdocdate: October 5 2026 $
.Dt CSHEET-MCP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm csheet-mcp
.Nd Model Context Protocol server for reading code cheat sheets from a Markdown document.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f Ar FILE
.Op Fl v
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar FILE
cheat sheet Markdown file
.It Fl v
display version
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server which exposes the cheat sheets read by
.Xr csheet 1
to MCP clients. It communicates using JSON-RPC over standard input and output.
.Pp
By default
.Ql ~/csheet.md
is read, but this can be overruled by adding
.Op Fl f Ar FILE
to specify the Markdown file. The file is not created when it does not exist.
.Pp
The following tools are provided:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It list_entries
list all entries as
.Ql subject section ,
optionally filtered by the argument
.Ar subject
.It get_entry
return the content of the entry identified by the arguments
.Ar subject
and
.Ar section
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss Configure an MCP client
.Bd -literal
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "csheet": {
      "command": "csheet-mcp",
      "args": ["-f", "/home/user/other.md"]
    }
  }
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr csheet 1
